{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49123","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:53.692836+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Internal reproducer submitted in cl/985128558.","created_at":"2026-09-21T09:30:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49123#issuecomment-5758322202","id":5758322202,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49123","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABVzkGGg","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5758322202/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-21T09:30:42Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5758322202","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194224583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penumallas1261","id":194224583,"login":"penumallas1261","node_id":"U_kgDOC5Ohxw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"## Summary\n\nAn `s8` convolution with `feature_group_count=2` produces a wrong value in the second group on XLA:GPU. A 1×1 kernel with 4 input channels, 4 output channels and 2 groups can be used, we see the last output channel is wrong and 3×3 spatial extents are wrong too. XLA:CPU, `float32` inputs, and `feature_group_count` 1 or 4 are all correct, so the issue is specific to the int8 grouped path dispatched to `__cudnn$convForward`. \n\n## Reproducer\n\n```python\nimport os; os.environ.setdefault(\"XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE\", \"false\")\nimport numpy as np, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\n\ndef grouped_conv(x, w, groups):                          # NCHW / OIHW, 1x1 kernel, stride 1, no padding\n    return lax.conv_general_dilated(x, w, (1, 1), \"VALID\", feature_group_count=groups)\n\ndef reference(x, w, groups):\n    N, C, H, W = x.shape; O, Cg = w.shape[:2]; Og = O // groups\n    out = np.zeros((N, O, H, W), np.int64)\n    for g in range(groups):\n        out[:, g*Og:(g+1)*Og] = np.einsum(\"nchw,oc->nohw\", x[:, g*Cg:(g+1)*Cg].astype(np.int64), w[g*Og:(g+1)*Og, :, 0, 0].astype(np.int64))\n    return ((out + 128) % 256 - 128).astype(np.int8)      # int8 wraparound, matching the int8 output\n\nx = (np.arange(4).reshape(1, 4, 1, 1) % 5 - 2).astype(np.int8)          # [[-2],[-1],[0],[1]]\nw = ((np.arange(8).reshape(4, 2, 1, 1) * 3) % 7 - 3).astype(np.int8)    # 4 output channels, 2 groups of 2 input channels\nexpected = reference(x, w, 2)\nfor dev in {d.platform: d for d in jax.devices() + jax.devices(\"cpu\")}.values():\n    with jax.default_device(dev):\n        out = np.asarray(jax.jit(grouped_conv, static_argnums=2)(jnp.asarray(x), jnp.asarray(w), 2))\n    print(f\"{dev.platform}: got={out.ravel().tolist()} expected={expected.ravel().tolist()} {'ok' if np.array_equal(out, expected) else 'WRONG'}\")\n```\n\n```\ngpu: got=[6, -5, -2, 1] expected=[6, -5, -2, -3] WRONG\ncpu: got=[6, -5, -2, -3] expected=[6, -5, -2, -3] ok\n```\n\nOutput channel 3 should be `w[3] · x[2:4] = (-3)·0 + (−3)·1 = −3`; the GPU returns `1`.\n\n## Agent Analysis\n\nThe optimized GPU HLO is semantically correct up to the custom call: the four-channel input is padded and dispatched as\n`custom_call_target=\"__cudnn$convForward\"`, `feature_group_count=2`, `\"algorithm\":{\"algo_id\":\"28\",\"is_cudnn_frontend\":false}`. The wrong values are produced inside that call, so the defect is in the int8 grouped-convolution lowering (`cudnn_fused_conv_rewriter` / `cudnn_vectorize_convolutions` layout and filter handling for `feature_group_count > 1`) or in the chosen cuDNN algorithm for this configuration. Requesting `preferred_element_type=jnp.int32` instead turns the same convolution into a loud `UNIMPLEMENTED: Can't lower one or more integer convolutions to idioms supported by CuDNN`, so the s8→s8 grouped path is the only one that runs, and it runs wrong.\n\n","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49123/comments","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:51:30Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49123/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49123","id":5513848677,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":4409976544,"name":"bug","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/bug"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"008672","default":false,"description":"Awaiting response from openxla-eng","id":4409976552,"name":"stat:awaiting openxla-eng","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABBtrm6A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/labels/stat:awaiting%20openxla-eng"},{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"34E43D","default":false,"description":"XLA on Nvidia GPU","id":4432379563,"name":"NVIDIA-GPU","node_id":"LA_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABCDC-qw","url":"ht